r_q1\": \"<Respond to the Question 1 with the corresponding letter numbering>\",\n\"answer_q2\": \"<Respond to the Question 2 with the corresponding letter numbering>\"\n\n    }\n``` \n    \n\n## Scenario\nI was going on a date last week and desperately needed a formal shirt. I asked George if I could borrow his. He lent me his favorite shirt, which he thought was irreplaceable since it was given to him by his mother. During the date, I got some cake on the shirt and couldn't wash it off. I looked it up, and it turns out I could buy the same shirt for a couple of bucks. So, I decided just to buy him a new shirt to replace it. I bet he won't mind.\n\n## Question 1\nWhat emotion(s) would George ultimately feel in this situation?\n\n## Choices for Question 1\nA) Gratitude & Guilt\nB) Disappointment & Guilt\nC) Anger & Disappointment\nD) Gratitude & Embarrassment\nE) Embarrassment & Guilt\nF) Unbothered & Disappointment\n\n## Question 2\nWhy would George feel these emotions in this situation?\n\n## Choices for Question 2\nA) I ruined his favorite shirt & I asked to borrow his shirt\nB) I went on a date without him & I told his mom about the shirt\nC) I ruined his favorite shirt & I went on a date without him\nD) I ruined his favorite shirt & I offered to buy a new shirt to replace his old shirt without considering its value\nE) I offered to buy a new shirt to replace his old shirt without considering its value & I asked to borrow his shirt\nF) I asked to borrow his shirt & I could afford to buy a new shirt but still borrowed his","options":null,"imageContent":null,"audioContent":null,"videoContent":null,"reminderContext":null,"videoCoverUrl":null,"chips":null,"customMessage":null,"media":null,"mediaTime":null,"interceptContent":null,"contents":[],"imgs":null,"regenerations":0,"seqNum":2,"responseSource":"agent:llm","isSuicide":false,"isSuicideConf":0.0075741987880470225,"emotions":[],"relationId":"6af5a0b79aa9dc5a833d8d9c","courseProgressId":0,"tsGen":1794482359043,"cre